  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 349 AM EST Sun Nov 15 2026\n\nAll in all, the long term period (Monday Night through Saturday) \nshould be largely uneventful for North and Central Georgia. Another \nshortwave trough will be activity swing through the ArkLaMiss and \ndriving a low pressure system across the northern Gulf Coast while \npushing eastward. Still noting most of the moisture associated with \nthis system will be displace well to our south. By mid-week and as \nthis system departs, strong high pressure builds and extends south \ninto the TN Valley/Southeast states. Similarly, amplified mid-level \nridging will build and remain the primary driver of the weather \npattern across the Southeast through the weekend. The net effects of \nhigh pressure and ridging aloft will keep us mostly dry and \ntemperatures trending warmer each day. Expect low temperatures to \nrise back above freezing around mid-week with forecast values in the \n40s to near 50. Daytime temperatures will behave similarly, starting \noff in the 50s to near 60s, warming into the 70s by the end of the \nweek.",
